   f(2) = 5(2^3) - 2(2) + 3 = 5(8) - 2(2) + 3 = 40 - 2(2) + 3 = 41
   \end{equation*}

Therefore, when $x = 2$, the value of the function $f(x) = 5x^3 - 2x + 3$ is $41$.

